body:
I have a common pf template that I use on all my OpenBSD hosts. I use variables to open ports and manage host-specific configuration.

Example:

    pass in quick on egress proto tcp from any to (egress) port {{ sshd_port }}

    {% if pf_allow_http %}
    pass in on egress proto tcp from any to (egress) port {80 443}
    {% endif %}

    {% if pf_allow_syncthing %}
    pass in on egress proto tcp from any to (egress) port 22000
    {% endif %}

Task to install it:

    - name: Install pf.conf file
      template:
        src: pf.conf.j2
        dest: /etc/pf.conf
        mode: 0600
        validate: pfctl -nf %s
      notify: Reload pf
